{"id":"word:hebrew:H7043","type":"word","title":"קָלַל","subtitle":"H7043 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to be (causatively, make ) light , literally ( swift , small , sharp , etc.) or figuratively ( easy , trifling , vile , etc.)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to קָלַל (H7043) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 82 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"קָלַל (qâlal) means to be (causatively, make ) light , literally ( swift , small , sharp , etc.) or figuratively ( easy , trifling , vile , etc.) First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 2 8."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"קָלַל","transliteration":"qâlal","pronunciation":"kaw-lal'","strong":"H7043","lemmaId":"hebrew:H7043","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["הָקֵל֩","הָקֵל֙","הָקֵ֣ל","וַ/יְקַלֵּ֔ל","קִלֵּ֖ל"],"morphs":[["HVhv2ms",6],["HVqp3cp",5],["HVpi3ms",5],["HC/Vpw3ms",4],["HTi/VNp3ms",2],["HVNp3ms",2],["HC/Vprmsa",2],["HR/Vpc/Sp3ms",2],["HVpp3ms",2],["HVlp3ms",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"to be (causatively, make ) light , literally ( swift , small , sharp , etc.) or figuratively ( easy , trifling , vile , etc.)","usage":"abate, make bright, bring into contempt, (ac-) curse, despise, (be) ease(-y, -ier), (be a, make, make somewhat, move, seem a, set) light(-en, -er, -ly, -ly afflict, -ly esteem, thing), × slight(-ly), be swift(-er), (be, be more, make, re-) vile, whet.","full":"H7043. qalal [ קָלַל ] 82 verb be slight, swift, trifling (probably originally be light ; Late Hebrew [ קָלַל ], קִלֵּל קַל, =Biblical Hebrew; Assyrian ‡alâlu II. depise, dishonour ; so Tel Amarna (apparently Canaanism); Arabic be small, scanty ; Sabean קללם scanty Hal 143.8f. (compare Fell ZMG liv (1900), 246 ); Ethiopic be light, Small, easy ; II. despise ; Targum קְלַל , Syriac = Biblical Hebrew; also (see Pilpel , etc.) Arabic shake , : vibrate, whirl (of sword), : see be shaken ; — Schw ZAW xi (1891), 170 ff. thinks shake original, see מַקֵּל ); — Qal Perfect 2masculine singular קַלּוֺתָ Nahum 1:14 ; 1 singular קַלֹּתי Job 40:4 ; 3 plural קַלּוּ Gen 8:11 +; Imperfect . 3 feminine singular וַתֵּקַל 16:4 ; 1 singular וָאֵקַל 16:5 ; 3 masculine plural יֵָ֑קלּוּ 1Sam 2:30 ; &#8212; 1 be slight , of water, be abated , fr off ( מֵעַל ) earth Gen 8:8 , 11 (J). 2 be swift , with מִן compare, of warriors 2Sam 1:23 , horses Jer 4:13 ; Hab 1:8 ; one's days Job 7:6 ; 9:25 . 3 trifling , i.e. of little account., of person, Gen 16:4-5 , (J; both with בְּעֵינֶיהָ ; 1Sam 2:30 (opposed to אֲכַבֵּד ). Niph`al Perfect 3masculine singular נָקֵל (Ges §67 t.) 2 Kings 20:30 +, וְנָקַל consecutive 2Kin 3:18 ; נָקָ֑ל Prov 14:6 ; 1 singular consecutive וּנְקַלֹּתִי 2Sam 6:22 ; Imperfect 3masculine plural יִקַּ֫לּוּ Isa 30:16 ; Participle feminine נְקַלָּה ( עַלֿ ) Jer 6:14 : + 2t ; — 1 shew oneself swift Isa 30:16 (|| נִרְכָּ֑ב עַלקַֿל ). 2 appear trifling , 1Sam 18:23 ( בְּעֵינֵיכֶם ; Infinitive subject, compare Dr), with מִן compare be too trifling Isa 49:6 , especially of sin 1Kin 16:31 (Infinitive subject), and (with מִן compare) Ezek 8:17 ; easy 2Kin 3:18 ( בְּעֵנַי ), 20:10 (c. Infinitive), Prov 14:6 ; Participle (as substantive) with עַל in adverb phrase עַלנְֿקַלָּה lightly i.e. superficially, Jer 6:14 ; 8:11 . 3 be lightly esteemed 2Sam 6:22 (|| שָׁפָל ; opposed to אִכָּכֵ֑דָה ). Pi`el 40 Perfect 3masculine singular קִלֵּל 2Sam 19:22 +, etc.; Imperfect יְקַלֵּל Lev 20:9 +, etc : Imperative masculine singular קַלֵּל 2Sam 16:10 ; Infinitive construct קַלֵּל Gen 8:21 : Josh 24:9 , etc.; Participle מְקַלֵּל Exod 21:17 +; suffix מקללוני כֻלֹּה Jer 15:10 , read מְקַלְלַוְנִי ! (Baer); error for קִלְלוּנִי כֻּלְּהֶם JDMich Gf Gie Du and others, etc.; — curse (properly make contemptible ): 1 with accusative of person homin. Exod 21:27 (E), Gen 12:3 (J), Lev 19:14 (H), Judg 9:27 ; 2Sam 16:9 16 t.; קְלָלָה קִלְלַנִי 1Kin 2:8 ; object omitted 2Sam 16:5 , 7 , 10 , 11 , 13 ; Psa 62:5 ; 109:28 (opposed to בֵּרַךְ ); acc person + ב of oath 1Sam 17:43 ; 2Kin 2:24 ; with כ of oath alone Isa 8:21 . 2 with accusative dei Exod 22:27 (E), Lev 24:15 (H), 1Sam 3:13 (reading אֱלֹהִים for ᵐ5 להֶם Comm.), + (object omitted) Lev 24:11 , 14 , 23 3 with accusative of thing Gen 8:21 ( ׳י subject), Job 3:1 . Pu`al Imperfect ) 3 masculine singular יְקֻלָּ֑ל Isa 65:20 be cursed by death; 3 feminine singular תְּקֻלַּל Job 24:18 their portion is cursed ; Participle plural suffix מְקֻלָּלָיו Psa 37:22 = those cursed by him (opposed to מְברָכָיו ). Hiph`il Perfect 3masculine singular הֵקַל Isaiah 8:23; 2 masculine singular suffix הֱקִלֹּחַנִי 2 Samuel 19:44 (van d. H. - הֲ ); 3 plural הֵקַלּוּ Ezek 22:7 ; Imperfect 3masculine singular יָקֵל 1Sam 6:5 ; Imperative masculine singular; הָקֵל Exod 18:22 +; Infinitive construct id. , Isa 23:9 ; Jonah 1:5 ; &#8212; 1 make light, lighten , מֵעֲלֵיכֶם אֶתיָֿדוֺ יָקֵל 1Sam 6:5 ; he will lighten his hand from upon you ; c,. מֵעַל person alone, make light from upon one, lighten one's burden Exod 18:22 (E), Jonah 1:5 ; 1Kin 12:10 2Chr 10:10 ; + מִן partitive 1Kin 12:4 , 9 2Chr 10:4 , 9 . 2 treat with contempt , accusative of person 2 Samuel 19:44; Isa 23:9 ; Ezek 22:7 ; direct causative bring contempt, dishonour Isaiah 8:23 (opposed to הִכְבִּיד ). Pilpel Perfect 3masculine singular 1 shake בַּחצִּים קִלְקַל Ezek 21:26 (in divination). 2 (peculiarly) whet Eccl 10:10 (properly move quickly to and fro). Hithpalpel reflexive of 1 : Perfect 3plural הִחְקַלְקָ֑לוּ Jer 4:24 hills shook themselves , shook.","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 2 8","keyReferences":["1Kgs 2 8","1Kgs 12 4","1Kgs 12 9","1Kgs 12 10","1Kgs 16 31","1Sam 2 30","1Sam 3 13","1Sam 6 5"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":82,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 2 8","book":"1Kgs","chapter":2,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceW